1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,280
Good morning. This is Burnham tourist office, Martin speaking.

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:10,229
Oh, hello. I saw a poster about free things to do in the area,

3
00:00:10,229 --> 00:00:13,410
and it said people should phone you for information.

4
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:16,160
I'm coming to Burnham with my husband

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:20,329
and two children for a few days on June the 27th,

6
00:00:20,329 --> 00:00:26,480
or possibly the 28th, and I'd like some ideas for things to do on the 29th.

7
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:31,680
Yes, of course. OK. Then let's start with a couple of events especially for children.

8
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,504
The art gallery is holding an event called 'Family Welcome' that day,

9
00:00:35,504 --> 00:00:39,010
when there are activities and trails to use throughout the gallery.

10
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:42,460
That sounds interesting. What time does it start?

11
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:43,940
The gallery opens at 10

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:47,480
and the 'Family Welcome' event runs from 10.30 until 2 o'clock.

13
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,405
The gallery stays open until 5.

14
00:00:49,405 --> 00:00:52,300
And several times during the day

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,180
they're going to show a short film that the gallery has produced.

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,182
It demonstrates how ceramics are made,

17
00:00:57,182 --> 00:01:01,520
and there'll be equipment and materials for children to have a go themselves.

18
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:04,833
Last time they ran the event, there was a film about painting,

19
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:06,960
which went down very well with the children

20
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,250
and they're now working on one about sculpture.

21
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:14,610
I like the sound of that. And what other events happen in Burnham?

22
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:16,730
Well, do you all enjoy listening to music?

23
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:17,820
Oh, yes.

24
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:21,275
Well there are several free concerts taking place at different times -

25
00:01:21,275 --> 00:01:26,300
one or two in the morning, the majority at lunchtime, and a couple in the evening.

26
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,110
And they range from pop music to Latin American.

27
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:32,790
The Latin American could be fun. What time is that?

28
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:35,740
It's being repeated several times, in different places.

29
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,443
They're performing in the central library at 1 o'clock,

30
00:01:38,443 --> 00:01:43,380
then at 4 it' s in the City Museum, and in the evening, at 7

31
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:45,350
30, there's a longer concert, in the theatre.

32
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:48,800
Right. I'll suggest that to the rest of the family.

33
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,300
Something else you might be interested in is the boat race along the river.

34
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,830
Oh, yes, do tell me about that.

35
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:57,100
The race starts at Offord Marina

36
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,240
to the north of Burnham, and goes as far as Summer Pool.

37
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:03,300
The best place to watch it from is Charlesworth Bridge

38
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,000
though that does get rather crowded.

39
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,920
And who's taking part?

40
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:10,270
Well, local boat clubs, but the standard is very high.

41
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:14,791
One of them came first in the West of England regional championship in May this year -

42
00:02:14,791 --> 00:02:17,900
it was the first time a team from Burnham has won.

43
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:22,510
It means that next year they'll be representing the region in the national championship.

44
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:28,500
Now I've heard something about Paxton Nature Reserve

45
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:32,210
It's a good place for spotting unusual birds, isn't it?

46
00:02:32,210 --> 00:02:33,708
That's right - throughout the year.

47
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:36,420
There is a lake there, as well as a river

48
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,800
and they provide a very attractive habitat.

49
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,710
So it's a good idea to bring binoculars if you have them.

50
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:46,012
And just at the moment you can see various flowers that are pretty unusual -

51
00:02:46,012 --> 00:02:49,700
the soil at Paxton isn't very common. They're looking good right now.

52
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:54,080
Right. My husband will be particularly interested in that.

53
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:57,532
And there is going to be a talk and slide show about mushrooms -

54
00:02:57,532 --> 00:03:00,200
and you'll be able to go out and pick some afterwards

55
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,780
and study the different varieties.

56
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:06,000
Uhuh. And is it possible for children to swim in the river?

57
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,690
Yes. Part of it has been fenced off to make it safe for children to swim in.

58
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,590
It's very shallow, and there's a lifeguard on duty whenever it's open.

59
00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:16,700
The lake is too deep, so swimming isn't allowed there.

60
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:21,740
OK, we must remember to bring their swimming things, in case we go to Paxton.

61
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:25,450
How long does it take to get there by car from Burnham?

62
00:03:25,450 --> 00:03:28,063
About 20 minutes, but parking is very limited,

63
00:03:28,063 --> 00:03:33,290
so it's usually much easier to go by bus - and it takes about the same time.

64
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:37,780
Right. Well, I'll discuss the options with the rest of the family

65
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:40,150
Thanks very much for all your help.

66
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:40,760
You're welcome.

67
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:41,670
Goodbye.

68
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:42,780
Bye.
